1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
This is a replay of the install, drawn
from recorded text. It is not a screen
recording.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Open Terminal on a Mac, or PowerShell on
Windows. You will type claude to open
Claude Code.

3
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:28,000
First, update Claude Code. You need
version 2.1.300 or newer.

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Now type claude. That opens Claude Code.
The rest happens inside it.

5
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:45,000
In Claude Code, add the Golden Thread
marketplace, using your team's GitHub
address.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Install gt-all. It brings gt and every
module with it.

7
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Restart Claude Code by typing exit and
then claude again. Then run gt-setup.

8
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Pick Install everything. It is the
recommended answer.

9
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:20,000
For the other questions, take the
recommended answer.

10
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:30,000
To leave a module out, choose Choose
modules, or run gt-setup again later.

11
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Restart Claude Code once more. Installing
a module turns none of its behavior on.

12
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Ask Claude for the gt help page. It shows
every command, and plays each one in a
simulated terminal.

13
00:01:51,000 --> 00:02:03,000
gt also puts a column of buttons beside
the chat. Press one, and Claude does the
task for you.

14
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Links to the install guide, the manual and
the getting started guide are on screen.
Inside Claude, gt-help is always there.
